{title: Arise, My Love}
{subtitle: Song of Songs 2}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 82}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Dm] | ×9
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The voice of my beloved, look, he comes
Leaping o[Gm]ver the mountains, bounding o[Dm]ver the hills
My beloved speaks and says to me
Arise, [C]my love, my beautiful [Bb]one, [C]and come a[Dm]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For be[Bb]hold, the [C]winter is [Dm]past
The rain is [C]over and [Dm]gone
The flowers [Bb]ap[C]pear on the [Dm]earth
The time of [C]singing has [Dm]come
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
The fig tree ripens its figs
The vines are in [Gm]blossom, they give their [Dm]fragrance
Arise, my love, my beautiful one
And come a[C]way
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
For be[Bb]hold, the [C]winter is [Dm]past
The rain is o[C]ver and [Dm]gone
The flowers ap[Bb]pear [C]on the [Dm]earth
The time of sin[C]ging has [Dm]come
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Gm] | [Gm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] |
